# Part 5, row 4: `.must()`, `.default(v)` and `.is_err()`. All three read the
# tag of a `T?` (row 5: a built-in variant, `ok` at 0 and `err` at 1) — and
# only two of them need an edge, which is why `is_err` is the cheap one.
function widen(v: int?) -> int
    if v.is_err()
        return v.default(0)
    return v.must()
